$ pace begin --at soon   # at 09:30
success: false
exit_code: 2
----- stdout -----

----- stderr -----
  × `soon` is not a time pace understands
  help: use `HH:MM`, `yesterday HH:MM`, `YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM` or a time back from now like `-15m`


$ pace begin --at 10:00   # at 09:30
success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Began [ID-1] at 2026-11-25 10:00.
pace keeps its data in [SANDBOX]/home.

----- stderr -----

$ pace begin --at +15m   # at 09:30
success: false
exit_code: 2
----- stdout -----

----- stderr -----
  × `+15m` lies in the future
  help: did you mean `-15m`?


$ pace begin --at -15m   # at 09:30
success: true
exit_code: 0
----- stdout -----
Ended [ID-1] at 09:15 after 23h 15m.
Began [ID-2] at 09:15.

